class.description:
[TextLocalizationServer] is the text server of the localization system and replaces [TranslationServer] for game code. It reads [TextLocalizationCatalog]s (see [LocalizationServer] for layers, priorities and the locale chain).
On a locale or catalog change it builds one resolved column for the active locale chain: one text per key. [method translate] is then one hash lookup and one array read, [method translate_id] one array read. Texts are [String]s, not [StringName]s.
[b]tr() keeps working:[/b] while the server has catalogs, one adapter [Translation] per channel domain answers [method Object.tr], [method Node.atr], [member Node.auto_translate_mode], [method TranslationServer.translate] and their plural forms from the same column, for the keys of that channel: the catalogs of the [code]interface[/code] channel in the main [TranslationDomain], those of [code]subtitles[/code] in the domain [code]"subtitles"[/code] (nodes with [method Object.set_translation_domain] [code]"subtitles"[/code]), and so on. Pseudolocalization and POT generation work as before.
[b]Channels:[/b] every key is translated in the locale of its channel ([method TranslationServer.get_locale_for]); a change of one channel rebuilds only its keys.
[b]Missing texts:[/b] a key without a text in the chain returns the key itself. In debug builds [signal key_missing] is emitted once per key and locale.
[b]Placeholders:[/b] when [code]args[/code] is not empty, [code]{name}[/code] placeholders are filled with [method TextInsertionServer.insert_template]; the parsed template is cached per key. Without [code]args[/code] the text is returned as it is (use [method TextInsertionServer.insert] to fill global values).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var title = TextLocalizationServer.translate(&"MENU_TITLE")
var open = TextLocalizationServer.translate(&"OPEN", &"door")
var apples = TextLocalizationServer.translate(&"APPLES", &"", count, { "n": count })

# Hot code: look the key up once, then translate by id.
var gold_id = TextLocalizationServer.get_key_id(&"HUD_GOLD")
label.text = TextLocalizationServer.translate_id(gold_id, -1, { "gold": gold })
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
string title = TextLocalizationServer.Translate("MENU_TITLE");
string open = TextLocalizationServer.Translate("OPEN", "door");
string apples = TextLocalizationServer.Translate("APPLES", "", count, new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "n", count } });

// Hot code: look the key up once, then translate by id (no StringName conversion per call).
int goldId = TextLocalizationServer.GetKeyId("HUD_GOLD");
label.Text = TextLocalizationServer.TranslateId(goldId, -1, new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "gold", gold } });
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
